criteria:
Inclusion criteria:
1. Male or female patients aged 18-70.
2. Total bilirubin must be < 2.0 x the upper limit of normal (ULN) unless known Gilbert syndrome
3. ALT or AST must be < 3 x the upper limit of normal.
4. Female patients: if postmenopausal for at least 1 year before enrolment or, if fertile - agreeing to practice 2 effective methods of contraception or agreeing to practice true abstinence.
5. Male patients should agree to practice barrier contraception or to practice abstinence
6. Treatment-naïve, classical HL patients with Ann Arbor stage I or II A non-bulky disease stratified according  to modified  EORTC Criteria (refer to Appendix A);
7. Patients must have histologically confirmed classical HL according to the current World Health Organization Classification (nodular sclerosis, mixed cellularity, lymphocytes rich, lymphocytes depleted, or classical HL NOS [not otherwise specified];
8. ECOG performance status 0-2
9. Hemoglobin must be > 8 gr./dL
10. Absolute neutrophil count ≥ 1,000/μL
11. Platelet count ≥ 100,000/μL
12. Voluntary written consent to take part to the study
13. Serum Creatinine < 2.0 mg/dL and/or Creatinine clearance or calculated Creatinine clearance > 40 mL/minute
Exclusion criteria:
1. Composite lymphoma or nodular lymphocyte-predominant Hodgkin lymphoma;
2. Severely impaired, lung and renal function;
3. Diagnosed or treated for another malignancy within 3 years before the first dose or previously diagnosed with another malignancy and have any evidence of residual disease. Patients with non-melanoma skin cancer or carcinoma in situ of any type are not excluded if they have undergone complete resection;
4. Active autoimmune disorder in treatment with immunosuppressive drugs
5. A left-ventricular ejection fraction < 50%;
6. Myocardial infarction within 2 years of study entry.
7. Pregnancy or lactation
8. Bulky disease (Lugano 2014 definition: single or conglomerated nodal mass with the largest diameter measuring 10 or more centimeters);
9. B symptoms;
10. Extra nodal site involved by disease;
11. Female patients who are both lactating and breastfeeding or who have a positive serum pregnancy test during the screening period or a positive pregnancy test on Day 1 before first dose of study drug;
12. Uncompensated diabetes mellitus requiring insulin therapy;
13. Any serious medical or psychiatric illness that could, in the investigator's opinion, potentially interfere with the completion of treatment according to this protocol;
14. Known human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection with a positive search for HIV antigens by immunoblot and/or circulating copies of HIV-RNA;
15. Active hepatitis B with circulating copies of HBV-DNA, or active hepatitis C infection with circulating copies of HCV-RNA;
